<title>SINGAPORE: Goodwood Park six-mth net up 20.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Goodwood Park six-mth net up 20.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  27.14    vs     22.59</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)	    55.00    vs     50.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	 60.00    vs     50.00</p>
<p>    Turnover		   161.62    vs    143.77</p>
<p>    Investment income	 80.17    vs     81.97</p>
<p>    Other income		 0.19    vs	0.02</p>
<p>    Interest expense	  13.81    vs	7.36</p>
<p>    Depreciation		 7.03    vs	4.02</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	    41.19    vs     35.04</p>
<p>    Tax			   10.70    vs	9.04</p>
<p>    Minorities		   3.35    vs	3.41</p>
<p>Dividend pay/ register - June 6 1997 / May 28 1997</p>
<p>Note - Goodwood Park Hotel Ltd said despite keen competition in the hotel industry and potentially lower second half profits from investments, the group's full year profit was not expected to be less than that of last year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
